      "content": "To reach 3NF, you first need to identify all non-key columns that depend on more than just the primary key through a transitive relationship (i.e., A → B and B → C, implying A → C). Next, create a new table for each such dependent attribute, moving those attributes to a table linked only to the intermediate entity. Finally, your original table should retain only the primary key and any direct non-key attributes, ensuring no non-prime attribute depends on another non-prime attribute. This process eliminates redundant data and ensures full dependency normalization.",
